statement:
Let n ∈ ℕ, R, E ∈ ℝ, B := B̆_R(0) ⊆ ℝⁿ (ℝⁿ = Euclid n), e_i := EuclideanSpace.single i 1, and D = fderiv ℝ. Assume:
- u_j : ℝⁿ → ℝ (j ∈ ℕ) is Lipschitz with ∫_B ‖Du_j‖² ≤ E for every j;
- c_j ∈ ℝ;
- W ∈ L²(B) (MemLp W 2 for Lebesgue measure restricted to B), and ∫_B (u_j − c_j − W)² → 0;
- h : ℝⁿ → ℝ is of class C¹ on B, with h = W almost everywhere on B;
- Φ_0, …, Φ_{n−1} : ℝⁿ → ℝ are C¹, each with compact support and tsupport Φ_i ⊆ B.
Then ∫_B Σ_i Dh(x)(e_i)·Φ_i(x) dx ≤ √E·√(∫_B Σ_i Φ_i(x)² dx).
